  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">Output 8.2. Increased capacity of Member States to improve governance and sustainability of social protection systems</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">In October 2023, the government of Burundi completed the ILO Social Security Inquiry (SSI) to improve the statistical system and data on coverage of social protection programs. In its implementation, social security data for 2021 was collected using the tool. Within the framework and resources available under the ILO&#x2019;s Global Flagship Programme on Building Social Protection Floors for All, the ILO facilitated participation of the representatives from the Permanent Executive Secretariat of the National Social Protection Commission (SEP/CNPS) and the National Statistical centre (Burundi National of Institute Statistics) to participate in the ILO regional training on the collection and compilation of social protection coverage data using the ILO Social Security Inquiry (SSI) tool. The training was delivered both virtually and face-to-face during the period between April and June 2023. Participating organizations subsequently co-ordinated successfully collection of comprehensive data on different social protection schemes in Burundi. Further, the SEP/CNPS which includes representatives of social partners has approved the SSI excel version as the national reporting tool for all social protection programs which will ensure that information required by the online SSI will be available on a regular basis.</narrative>
   </description>
